{
  "case": "release notes from merged PRs",
  "variant": "without",
  "trial": 4,
  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 entry to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. The version and date come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files, and it follows the same format as the earlier entries:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n**Decision for you:** ACME-421 is marked `!` in the PR list, which means it's a breaking change, so I labelled it BREAKING and put it first. But `VERSION` only goes up a minor version (2.3.0 → 2.4.0). If you follow semver, removing a flag would usually mean 3.0.0. I left the version as it is; tell me if you want to bump it to 3.0.0 and I'll update the notes.\n\nI didn't include the PR authors (@mira, @jonas and others) because earlier entries don't name them. I can add them if you'd like.",
